  "findings": [
    "Pinned SDK server uses an eight-thread pool and releases the runtime execution lock during native callbacks. Some package-host instance helpers lack their own guard; this source observation is a hypothesis, not a demonstrated product crash cause.",
    "Initial same-process loopback probe stalled and ended naturally with five SDK call failures, 3000/8000 completed iterations and exit 1. Slow dump preserved. No process was killed. Its different topology/lifetime makes it unsuitable to establish the product heap-corruption cause.",
    "Separate-process probe passed eight simultaneous clients, each creating/calling 1000 native objects. Server and all clients exited zero.",
    "Qualified repeat freezes explicit SDK headers, source/helpers, diagnostics header, SDK DLL/import library, Node and CMake around build/run; all hashes/sets unchanged. Eight clients again complete all 8000 iterations.",
    "This simple factory/lifetime case did not reproduce product heap corruption. No SDK locking or runtime patch justified by this evidence."
  ],
  "scope": "Standalone native SDK diagnostics only. No xMind model/provider/tool work, SQLite task effects, installation or full product gate.",
